<!-- Website teaching layer for android/kotlin-multiplatform/ui-sharing/resource-sharing.md. Original preserved in full. Structure defined in android-phase9-structure.md before drafting. Checked 2026-10-25 against https://kotlinlang.org/docs/multiplatform/compose-multiplatform-resources-setup.html. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A translated string works in a developer build but is missing from the published consumer app. The accessor compiled, while the resource’s journey through generation and packaging was never checked. Both are part of the delivered contract.</p>

Follow one approved resource from its source to its actual reader, keeping native and shared UI ownership explicit.

<!-- @after Current Baseline :: visual -->
### One source can produce different platform outputs

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node"><strong>Canonical input</strong><small>Reviewed translations, assets and design-token schema</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Shared Compose surface</strong><small>Generated Kotlin resource API and packaged inputs</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Native surface</strong><small>Deliberately generated native catalog when appropriate</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Release proof</strong><small>Load the resource from the final consumer artifact</small></div></div><figcaption>Generated accessors establish names and types; they do not prove every deployment path included the assets.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after 6. Packaging, Publication, and Raw Files :: animation -->
### A string travels to the consumer

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">A string travels to the consumer</span><div class="stage viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node" data-el="n0"><strong>Approved catalog</strong><small data-text="v0">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="n1"><strong>Generation</strong><small data-text="v1">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="n2"><strong>Published artifact</strong><small data-text="v2">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="n3"><strong>Consumer app</strong><small data-text="v3">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[{"label": "Approve", "caption": "A reviewed translation includes its required placeholders and default value. Structural checks run before it becomes a build input.", "add": ["n0", "n1", "n2", "n3"], "state": {"n0": "active", "n1": "idle", "n2": "idle", "n3": "idle"}, "text": {"v0": "Versioned input", "v1": "Not generated", "v2": "Not packaged", "v3": "Old version"}}, {"label": "Generate", "caption": "The configured resource task generates supported accessors and target resources. Product callers use the declared API.", "add": ["n0", "n1", "n2", "n3"], "state": {"n0": "idle", "n1": "active", "n2": "idle", "n3": "idle"}, "text": {"v0": "Stable ownership", "v1": "Accessor + resource", "v2": "Build input ready", "v3": "Consumer still unverified"}}, {"label": "Package", "caption": "Publish the library through the supported integration path. Retain the intended public resource API and required payload.", "add": ["n0", "n1", "n2", "n3"], "state": {"n0": "idle", "n1": "idle", "n2": "active", "n3": "idle"}, "text": {"v0": "Traceable input", "v1": "Generated output", "v2": "Exact version", "v3": "Consumes that version"}}, {"label": "Verify", "caption": "Load the string in the final app under the required locale and text size. A library compile alone cannot establish correct packaging or layout.", "add": ["n0", "n1", "n2", "n3"], "state": {"n0": "idle", "n1": "idle", "n2": "idle", "n3": "active"}, "text": {"v0": "Source trace retained", "v1": "Contract checked", "v2": "Distribution tested", "v3": "Rendered and tested"}}]</script><figcaption>Illustrative sequence, not a measured trace. <a href="https://kotlinlang.org/docs/multiplatform/compose-multiplatform-resources-setup.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary contract</a>.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Common Failure Modes :: check -->
### Try the decision yourself

<details><summary>Does a public Res class prove a font was packaged?</summary><p>No. Verify runtime lookup in the final consumer artifact.</p></details>
<details><summary>Should the domain return translated copy?</summary><p>Keep domain outcomes separate from presentation-localization ownership where that boundary fits the product.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can one translation source serve native and shared UI?</summary><p>Yes, with deliberately generated target representations and validation; native catalogs are not automatically supplied by Kotlin accessors.</p></details>

